# Realtime Rules

Reference: `Project-X-Backend/src/services/realtime.service.js`, `Documents/decisions/notification-engine.md`

## Server

- Socket paths: `/realtime/socket.io`, `/api/realtime/socket.io`.
- All connections pass `authenticateSocket` — JWT from cookie, auth payload, or Bearer; same tenant policy as HTTP.
- Handshake `tenantSubdomain` follows `TENANT_RESOLUTION.md` (header/host mismatch → reject).
- Store `userId`, `role`, `tenantDbName` on `socket.data` after auth.

## Room naming

| Room | Pattern |
|------|---------|
| User (legacy fallback) | `user:{userId}` |
| Tenant user | `tenant:{tenantDbName}:user:{userId}` |
| Tenant broadcast | `tenant:{tenantDbName}` |
| Role | `tenant:{tenantDbName}:role:{roleId}` |
| Conversation | `tenant:{tenantDbName}:conv:{conversationId}` |

Prefer tenant-scoped rooms. Pass `{ tenantDbName }` in emit options when outside HTTP context.

## Event naming

Use `domain.action` lowercase dot notation:

- `notification.created`
- `task.status.changed`
- `timeEntry.changed`
- `chat.message.created`
- `chat.conversation.deleted`
- `interview.conversation.created`

New events must follow this pattern. Do not rename existing events without refactor-safety review.

## Emit helpers

Use `emitToUser`, `emitToTenant`, `emitToRole`, `emitToConversation` from `realtime.service.js` — never raw `io.emit` to all clients.

## Frontend / mobile

- Subscribe via `useRealtimeEvent(event, handler, enabled)` from `RealtimeProvider`.
- Disable polling (`refetchInterval`) when realtime is connected.
- Guard handlers: check `enabled && !!currentUser?._id`.
- Invalidate specific React Query keys — avoid full cache clears.
- Clean up: `useRealtimeEvent` must unregister on unmount (provider handles this).

## Do's

- Verify conversation membership before `chat:join` room joins.
- Limit `chat:join` batch size (max 200 IDs).
- Log auth failures with `[Realtime]` prefix when debugging.

## Don'ts

- Don't emit tenant-wide events without `tenantDbName`.
- Don't subscribe to the same event multiple times in one component tree.
- Don't add socket endpoints that skip tenant validation.
